{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966814,"nonce":"rdPoqhwJMgh+WyXsXEnmg/WlNzU=","title":"Portal-UI widget backlog tracks blinc_node_editor::config::PropertyDefinition variants. The","message":"**Source of truth for \"what widgets does portal_ui still need\":**\n`blinc_node_editor::config::PropertyDefinition` — one variant per\ncontent-slot field type. Each maps to the widget the inspector / node\ncontent slot renders. Anything not in this enum is host-rendered via\n`PropertyDefinition::Custom`.\n\n**Variant ↔ portal_ui widget status as of 2026-06-20:**\n\n| Variant | portal_ui widget | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| `Text` | `text_input` / `text_input_signal` | shipped, inline editing (click-to-focus, typed-char + Backspace / Delete / arrows / Home / End / Esc). Hosts wrap the canvas div with `install_kbd_hook(outer)`. Gaps: selection drag, clipboard, IME, cursor blink. |\n| `Textarea` | `textarea` | shipped (2026-06-20) — multi-line; Enter=newline, Up/Down between lines, `.rows(n)`, caret-follows scroll. Same `install_kbd_hook` requirement. |\n| `Number` | `numeric_input` + `slider` | shipped — `numeric_input` is drag-to-scrub OR click-to-edit with gauge fill, range/step/integer/precision/unit. |\n| `Boolean` | `switch` | shipped |\n| `Select` | `select_trigger` / `select` / `select_signal` | shipped (trigger only — caller opens overlay via `blinc_cn::context_menu`) |\n| `Color` | `color_picker` | shipped — chip trigger + `color_wheel_panel` overlay. |\n| `File` | `file_picker` | shipped (2026-06-20) — trigger chip (folder glyph + base name); overlay-escape, host opens the dialog on `resp.clicked` and writes the path back. |\n| `CodeEditor` | `button.icon` + `code_editor` overlay | shipped via demo recipe — inline preview chip opens `blinc_layout` code_editor in a popover. |\n| `Custom` | host-rendered | n/a |\n\n**Display / visualisation widgets (beyond PropertyDefinition):**\nall shipped — `chart` (line/bar/area), `pie_chart`, `radar_chart`,\n`wave_graph` (oscilloscope), `noise` (Perlin/Worley/Voronoi via\nblinc_noise), `texture` (ImageId + inline RGBA), `sdf_shape` (2D + 3D).\nAll support `.pip(true)`. Host-callable pure paint helpers exist for\nchart/pie/radar (`paint_chart` / `paint_pie` / `paint_radar` +\n`PortalPainter::for_host`) so overlays render the expanded PiP view\nWITH tooltips (cursor fed via `div().on_mouse_move`). noise / texture /\nsdf have NO for_host helper yet (no PiP-expand demand).\n\n**Genuinely remaining (all minor / optional):** text_input/textarea\ndrag-to-select SHIPPED 2026-06-20 (anchor+caret range, drag / shift+click /\nshift+arrow / shift+Up-Down, selection-replace edits, highlight rect;\nneeded core Response.click_shift + CLICKS cache carrying CanvasModifiers,\nsince the click event's modifiers only arrive on release — shift+click\nextends from a stashed pre_caret). STILL remaining: clipboard (Cmd+C/V/X),\nIME composition, Tab traversal between widgets, flexbox layout\n(only vertical/horizontal stacks today), noise-buffer cache in\nPortalStorage by params-hash (regenerated every paint now). The\nPropertyDefinition widget set is now COMPLETE (every variant has a\nnative portal_ui widget). Shadow plane is DONE (ShadowMix +\n`PortalStyle.buttons_shadow`).\n\n**Why:** the node-editor inspector + per-node content slot drives node\nmetadata / config / property values through `PortalUi`. Today only\nText + Boolean (via switch) + Number-as-slider work natively. Every\nother variant either falls back to read-only display or forces the\nhost to render via `Custom`, which kills the \"declarative\nPropertyDefinition → automatic inspector\" contract.\n\n**Inline text editing — how it works (shipped 2026-06-18):**\n\nThe plumbing did NOT extend `canvas_kit::InputState`. Instead,\n`blinc_portal_ui::ui::install_kbd_hook(div) -\u003e Div` attaches its\nown additive `on_key_down` + `on_text_input` handlers to the outer\ncanvas wrapper. Events land in two process-global buffers\n(`KBD_KEYS: Mutex\u003cVec\u003cKbdKey\u003e\u003e` and `KBD_CHARS: Mutex\u003cVec\u003cchar\u003e\u003e`),\ndrained by `Portal::frame` at the start of every paint and exposed\nto widgets via `PortalUi::keys_pressed()` / `chars_typed()`.\n\nGlobal focus state lives in `FOCUSED_REGION: Mutex\u003cOption\u003cString\u003e\u003e`\n(stores `widget_id.to_region_id(portal_id)`), set on click via\n`PortalUi::set_focus(WidgetId)` and cleared by `clear_focus()` or on\nEscape. `Response::widget_id` carries the stable id back to the\nwidget impl so `text_input` can persist its caret in\n`PortalStorage` keyed off the same id.\n\nTwo structural notes for future widget authors:\n\n1. `allocate_painter` holds `\u0026mut self.ctx` for the painter's\n   lifetime, so per-widget state work that touches `self.storage`,\n   `self.kbd_*`, or `self.set_focus` must happen BEFORE the\n   painter is allocated, or AFTER the painter scope drops. The\n   helper `PortalUi::allocate_painter_for_id` lets a widget\n   pre-compute its `WidgetId` (via `make_widget_id`), do its state\n   work, then paint with the same id — `text_input` is the\n   reference implementation.\n2. The `text_input` widget calls `ui.request_animation()` every\n   focused frame. This keeps the scheduler-bridge alive (see\n   gotcha portal ui scheduler bridge) and is what would\n   support cursor blink when we wire it. v0 paints a static caret\n   line.\n\n**Workaround for hosts that DON'T install the hook:** without\n`install_kbd_hook`, `text_input` still paints and reports clicks,\nbut the per-frame char / key buffers stay empty so typing does\nnothing. Hosts that want inline editing MUST install the hook\nonce on the outer div (idempotent against any other on_key_down\nhandler attached to the same div — handlers are additive).\n\n**How to apply / priority order for new work:**\n\n1. **Options dropdown (`Select`)** — anchor the popover via\n   `HostBridge::rect_to_screen` and let the host's overlay manager\n   own dismiss + z-order. Pattern is documented in README's \"Overlay\n   escape\" section. Lowest risk; no canvas-kit blocker.\n2. **Number input** — text-entry numeric field with up/down step\n   buttons. Same overlay-escape pattern as Text for the actual entry\n   widget (until keyboard routing lands), or skip text entry and ship\n   a stepper / drag-to-scrub interaction first.\n3. **Color picker** — canvas-paintable swatch + popover with HSV\n   picker. The picker itself is a portal-painted widget; the swatch\n   trigger is one-liner over `allocate_painter`.\n4. **Code editor inline** — reuse `blinc_layout::widgets::code_editor`\n   rendered into an overlay opened from a \"...\" trigger on the slot.\n   Don't try to host the full editor inside the canvas closure — its\n   widget tree is retained-mode and won't fit the immediate-mode\n   rhythm cleanly. Fallback: dialog overlay.\n5. Textarea + File can land as adjacent gaps once Text's keyboard\n   blocker resolves (they share the same input-routing path).\n6. **Charts** — generalised plot widget. Line chart + bar chart at\n   minimum; useful in node-editor for showing live signal output\n   from a node's evaluation. Axes + gridlines + tick labels are\n   `allocate_painter` primitives over `fill_rect` / `stroke_path` /\n   `draw_text`. Data API is a borrow over `\u0026[Point]` or `\u0026[(f32, f32)]`\n   so callers don't pay allocation per frame.\n7. **Wave graph** — specialisation of chart for time-series + audio.\n   X axis is time, Y is amplitude, with optional centre baseline for\n   bipolar signals (audio waveforms). Pattern after the README's\n   sparkline example but parameterised: configurable colour brush,\n   stroke width, optional fill-under, optional grid. Used by\n   node-editor nodes that emit per-frame samples (LFOs, envelope\n   followers, scope-style debug nodes).\n\nThese two are \"rich painted\" widgets — they live entirely inside\n`allocate_painter` and need no overlay escape. They unblock dataflow-\nstyle node editors where every node visualises its output inline.\n\n**Don't:** lean on `request_animation` for popover state without also\nregistering with the scheduler — see gotcha portal ui scheduler bridge.\nClick detection MUST use consume-on-read pattern, never timestamp\ncompare — see gotcha portal ui clicked consume on read.\n\n**Where the widget calls land:**\n- Inspector: `blinc_node_editor::inspector::InspectorField` reads\n  values out of the property and emits patches against `meta.key`.\n- Per-node content slot: `content_slot_rects` (in\n  `packages/blinc_node_editor/src/render.rs`) computes the\n  inset + portal rect; the node template's content closure paints\n  via `PortalUi` inside that rect.\n\n**Tested widgets (end-to-end, in node_editor_demo):**\n\n- `slider_signal` — Filter node's threshold slot\n- `switch_signal` — Formatter node's running toggle\n- `button.ghost()` — Filter node's \"Reset\" toolbar action\n- `button.destructive()` — Sink node's \"Clear\" button\n- `select_signal` + cn::context_menu overlay — Sink node's Format\n  dropdown\n- `text_input_signal` — Sink node's editable Label (added 2026-06-18)\n- (added 2026-06-18)\n\nAny new widget must land with a node_editor_demo content-slot\nexercise — paint + click + value mutation observable in the demo.\nDon't ship a widget that's only unit-tested.\n\n**Builder cascade shipped (2026-06-18):** every value-bearing\nwidget now follows the same shape as `ButtonBuilder`:\n- `SwitchBuilder` / `SliderBuilder` / `TextInputBuilder` accept\n  either `\u0026mut T` or `\u0026Signal\u003cT\u003e` via the sealed `PortalValue`\n  trait. One entry method per widget, `*_signal` retained as\n  `#[deprecated]` shims.\n- `SelectBuilder` (read-only, no value binding) covers\n  `select_trigger`, `select`, `select_signal` — all three return\n  the builder, all three terminate with `.show()` /\n  `.clicked()`.\n- `ShadowMix` trait centralises `.shadow_sm/.shadow_md/.shadow_lg/\n  .shadow_xl/.shadow_2xl/.shadow_inner/.shadow_default/\n  .shadow_none` shortcuts. Implementors only override\n  `.shadow(token)`. `ButtonBuilder` retrofits onto it.\n- `ValueBinding\u003cT\u003e` enum + `PortalValue` trait keep the unified\n  entry without duplicating builder types per \u0026mut/\u0026Signal.\n\n**Button variants shipped (2026-06-18):** `ButtonVariant` mirrors\n`cn::ButtonVariant` one-to-one (Primary / Secondary / Destructive /\nOutline / Ghost / Link). `button` returns a `ButtonBuilder` with\nfluent `.primary()` / `.destructive()` / `.ghost()` / `.outline()` /\n`.secondary()` / `.link()` / `.variant(v)` / `.disabled(b)`. Terminal\ncalls: `.show()` (Response), `.clicked()` / `.hovered()` /\n`.pressed()` / `.changed()` (bool shortcuts). DEFAULT variant is\n**Ghost**, NOT Primary — deliberate divergence from `cn::button`\nbecause portal buttons sit inside node bodies where a Primary fill\nwould dominate. See project portal ui cn parity rule.\n\n**Shadow tokens — not yet wired (follow-up):**\n`blinc_theme::tokens::ShadowToken` (Sm / Default / Md / Lg / Xl /\nXxl / Inner / None) and `ShadowTokens` exist in upstream Blinc; cn\nwidgets consume them via `box-shadow: theme(shadow-sm);` in CSS.\nPortal-UI widgets currently paint flat — no shadow plane. To match\ntheme expectations the right shape is:\n  1. Add `ShadowTokens` (or selected slots) to `PortalStyle` and\n     populate from `ThemeState::get().shadows()`.\n  2. Add `.shadow(ShadowToken)` builder on `ButtonBuilder` (and\n     later other variant-bearing widgets — popovers, cards if we\n     add them).\n  3. `PortalPainter` gains a helper that emits a box-shadow GPU\n     primitive at the painter's rect — Blinc's draw pipeline\n     already has a shadow primitive (used by cn). Render order:\n     emit shadow first, then bg fill / border / text.\n  4. Default `.shadow()` per variant:\n     - Primary / Secondary / Destructive → `Sm`\n     - Outline / Ghost / Link → `None`\n   so a hosted call `ui.button(\"Save\").primary().show()` carries\n   the standard CTA elevation without an explicit `.shadow()`.\nKeep cn-parity: variants pull from the same `ShadowToken` cn::button\nuses. Document any deliberate divergence (e.g. portal Ghost = no\nshadow even if cn Ghost has one).","files":null}]}